---
/**
 * The site's one loading placeholder, for a value that is fetched rather than
 * server-rendered.
 *
 * Why it exists: the lazy panels (Performance, Advertising) render their KPI
 * tiles before the data is fetched, and an unfilled number fell back to `0` /
 * `0%` / empty. A seller cannot tell a real zero from "not here yet" — they
 * read it as "I sold nothing" (owner, 2026-07-31: "מאיפה היוזר צריך לדעת שזה
 * טוען ולא אפס?"). A shimmer says "a number is coming" without ever stating a
 * wrong one.
 *
 * The shimmer itself is `.skel-bar` (utilities/utils.css) — the same treatment
 * every image grid on the site already uses, so this is the existing language,
 * not a new one. Sizing comes in as Tailwind utilities via `class`; the caller
 * matches the shape of the value it stands in for (a price bar is wider than a
 * count), because a placeholder that doesn't match its content causes a layout
 * jump the moment it's replaced.
 *
 * `aria-hidden` + the caller's `aria-busy`: a screen reader should hear "busy",
 * never a decorative bar. Every consumer clears `aria-busy` when the real value
 * lands (performance.ts → renderSummary).
 */
interface Props {
  /** Tailwind sizing utilities, e.g. "w-20 h-[1.15rem]". */
  class?: string;
}
const { class: className = '' } = Astro.props;
---
<span class:list={['skel-bar inline-block align-middle', className]} aria-hidden="true"></span>
